# Root project directory
KIRO*
/node_*
# Deploy configs carry real account, bucket and runtime identifiers — keep them local
# and commit only the placeholder templates (deploy/*.example.json). Same split as
# ../cold-agent, and for the same reason: the shapes are worth reviewing, the values
# are not worth publishing.
agent/deploy/*.json
!agent/deploy/*.example.json

# The agent half's local environment. `app/.gitignore` has covered `.env*` on its side
# since the foundation; `agent/` had no equivalent only because no `agent/.env` existed
# yet. It holds no credential today — the Azure secret and the progress token arrive in
# the invoke payload's `context`, never in the environment — but a file named `.env` is
# the wrong thing to leave trackable on that argument.
agent/.env
agent/.env.bak.*

# kiro-cli editor state, not project config
.kiro/settings/
